WEBVTT

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:04.920
Fly ball, right field!

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.940
Oota! When he has it, go!

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.590
<i>They got us.</i>

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:15.200
<i>Of </i>course<i> they'd send it out 
to the guy with the weak arm.</i>

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.350
<i>Bastards!</i>

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.910
<i>This is why I was against 
making that loser a regular!</i>

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.400
Here it is. His time to shine.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.160
Huh?

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.810
Go!

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.760
Please watch how much he has grown.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.510
Go!

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.680
Katsumoto, let it through!

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.540
That's far enough, Daigo-kun!

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:32.470
Yes, sir!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:38.170
Now I've Done It!

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.280
All right...

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.490
Now, I want you to throw it as though
you're throwing it back to home.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.670
Gotcha!

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.100
No, no, stop!

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.090
If you want to throw it back fast, 
especially all the way to home,

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:55.700
you need to start with your stance 
when catching the ball.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.570
When I'm catching it?

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:02.260
Daigo-kun, try throwing me 
a high fly ball from there.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.650
O-Okay.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.330
Watch my movements closely.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:11.600
First, stand about two or three steps 
behind where the ball's gonna drop.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:12.710
Dash forward!

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.340
Run on to the ball,

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:18.080
and catch it down to your right,
 so you can transition to throwing quicker.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.750
Then, use your body's forward 
momentum and throw!

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.840
I get it!

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.350
Running on to it will make up for my weak arm.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.280
That's right.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.390
Of course, there's also a trick 
to throwing the ball.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.490
Like I said before,

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:36.950
you'll almost never need to throw 
super long balls in an actual game.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.970
Same goes for practice. 
You only do them to warm up.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.450
Basically...

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.120
you want to throw the ball low and hard.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.550
Don't worry about not 
letting the ball bounce.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:54.400
A bouncing ball will reach home
faster than one with a high arc.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:58.130
There's also nothing wrong with using 
a relay man to get it back home.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:02.390
I don't have to worry about 
not letting the ball bounce?

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:03.520
Exactly.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:08.140
And your arm will get stronger if you keep 
practicing throwing the ball low and hard.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.580
I'll do it! I'll try my best!

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:17.650
There's not enough time before the game
 to properly build up your arm.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:19.320
However...

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:26.000
If you can throw the ball back 
quickly and accurately,

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.600
securing an out should be achievable, 
even if it is a bouncer.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.570
There's also a special step used by
outfielders called the "crow hop."

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:44.440
Once you've got the ball in your glove, 
leap forward and plant your left foot.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:47.400
As you feel your weight shifting forward,

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.380
put all of that momentum
into your throwing arm,

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.880
even at the risk of falling flat on your face!

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:56.690
Go!

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.890
Out!

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:05.720
That's three outs.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:06.360
Change sides!

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.370
He did it!

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.420
That was <i>amazing</i>, Shigeno-kun!

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:12.410
D-D-Daigo got him out?!

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:14.280
Nice one, Daigo!

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.410
Not bad, dude!

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:17.750
Wasn't expectin' that.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.420
It bounced twice,
but he got the ball back to me.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.150
He did it.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.960
Daigo-kun got him out.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.870
He threw the ball so hard, his cap fell off.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.040
Just like his pop.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:32.560
<i>Daigo...</i>

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:38.230
<i>When he quit baseball, he did 
nothing but play video games.</i>

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:42.360
<i>He always looked so miserable 
when I forced him to play.</i>

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.400
We did it!

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.630
<i>But look at him now!</i>

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.860
That play was awesome!

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.530
Yeah?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.080
Thank you so much, Satou-san.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.100
You've given that boy 
confidence, and for that,

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.590
I thank you from the bottom of my heart.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:03.460
I didn't do much. 
I just taught him some techniques.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:07.250
Making a play like that after 
only a short amount of training

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:09.220
is testament to the effort he put in.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.820
If he can keep up that attitude, he'll go far.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.030
That was amazing, Shigeno-kun!

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.220
Is that what you've been practicing?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.230
Mifune

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.230
Tanikawa

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.230
Foul!

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:18.810
Good try, Kimura.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:19.900
Keep fighting!

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:25.420
Ball.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:26.760
Ball four!

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.400
All right!

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.750
Our leadoff is on base!

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:32.340
We've got two innings left to play.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.650
If we can get another run this inning, 
we've got this in the bag!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.620
We're counting on you, Daigo!

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:38.800
Play!

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.220
<i>Ack! That went way too high.</i>

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.680
<i>Don't catch it!</i>

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.050
Out!

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:57.200
Great! The sacrifice bunt was a success.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.630
That was close!

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:03.120
It could've been an infield fly, 
but luckily, Kimura judged it well.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:03.770
Yeah.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.920
<i>I'm glad they didn't get the double play.</i>

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.100
Nice bunt.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:09.710
<i>Huh?</i>

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:13.380
<i>Did he just compliment me?</i>

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:15.770
<i>Yeah, right.</i>

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:18.400
<i>He was probably just being sarcastic.</i>

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.500
Play!

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:22.100
Go, Urabe!

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.750
<i>If we can rack up three wins and 
make it through to the quarters,</i>

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.960
<i>we might end up facing 
my old team, the Touto Boys.</i>

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:32.520
<i>If I have to flatter my pathetic 
teammates a bit to get there, so be it.</i>

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.680
<i>I cannot afford to lose!</i>

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.270
Yeah!

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.500
Stop, stop!

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.950
All right! One out, 
runners on first and third.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.950
Keep us rolling, Andy!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.010
<i>Come on, Andy.</i>

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:57.950
<i>To achieve our goals,</i>

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.960
<i>we can't waste time struggling 
against a foe this weak!</i>

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:21.730
W-Wow. He just casually 
knocked it out of the park.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.970
That's my partner, all right.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.330
I can always count on you.

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:28.920
We're up by four to nothing!

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:32.240
Now, all we've got to do is hang on 
to our lead for two more innings.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.230
Go finish this!

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:35.240
Yes, sir!

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.480
<i>I can't be afraid of errors.</i>

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:45.120
<i>And I can't make the same
mistake as last time.</i>

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.420
All right!

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.090
Nice one, Kishimoto!

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.600
<i>It's all or nothing!</i>

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:06.650
Out!

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:07.630
I did it!

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:09.520
Great job, Kimura!

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:11.660
They're doing really well!

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.580
They might just win this.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.150
Their defense has improved, hasn't it?

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:18.450
And they're communicating more.
Nothing but good vibes.

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:24.100
Foul.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:24.860
But...

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:27.840
The kid who's pitching is 
starting to look tired.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:28.460
Huh?

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.720
Guess he overexerted himself early on.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.420
The other team could hardly 
touch him at the start.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:37.420
But since the last inning, he's not 
been getting any swings and misses.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.350
Right field!

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:48.020
<i>Ah! I can't reach it!</i>

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.310
<i>Ack!</i>

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.690
Wh-What?!

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.500
Crap.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:58.740
It turned into a triple!

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.700
M-My bad.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:05.420
Sheesh, Daigo, what are you doing?

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:07.710
It wasn't really his fault.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.490
They're ahead by four,
and there were no runners.

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:12.650
Going for it wasn't a bad call.

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:14.460
He was just unlucky.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:18.220
Damn it.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.280
<i>I guess he's getting tired.</i>

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.910
<i>But we only need four more outs.</i>

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:26.480
<i>I don't care about this runner, 
but we can't let anyone else get on base!</i>

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:33.430
All right!

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:34.980
We're about to claw back a run!

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.120
Out!

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:48.060
Yes!

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.330
Nice one, Daigo-kun!

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:53.990
Daigo, that was amazing!

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:56.570
A grounder to right field,
and he got him out!

00:10:56.570 --> 00:11:00.090
What they did to him in the first inning
really wounded his pride.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.150
Out!

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:09.950
Since then, he's been waiting 
for an opportunity to get his revenge.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.580
Daigo-kun, great job!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.680
That kid's playing pretty well.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.810
Looks like he saved our butts again.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:17.990
Yeah.

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:22.030
He's a weird kid with zero consistency.
He swings from good to awful.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.990
But one thing's for sure:
 he's not riding Daddy's coattails.

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:38.220
We're finally in the last inning.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:40.550
And now, they've switched their pitcher.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.840
Switched from a lefty to a righty.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:46.000
Well, whatever. Doesn't look like 
he's anything to worry about.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.060
Yeah.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:57.650
Great. Our leadoff's 
made it to first again.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:01.180
<i>Up to now, I'm the only batter
 who hasn't done anything.</i>

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:04.460
<i>I need to get him to second 
on this first pitch.</i>

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:07.660
<i>I mean, even Daigo managed to do it.</i>

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:13.960
Out.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:18.290
Don't sweat it, Nagai.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:19.300
Thanks.

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:25.190
Yes!

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.890
One out, runners on first and second.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.040
This is our chance!

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.260
Keep us running, Kimura!

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:36.730
Ball.

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:38.020
Ball.

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:39.730
Ball.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.470
All right, three balls!

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:43.450
Keep your eyes on the ball, Kimura.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.740
This pitcher's all over the place.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:50.220
<i>Looks like I'm going to get a chance, too.</i>

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:54.000
<i>If all he can throw is lazy 90 kmph pitches,</i>

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:56.750
<i>I've got an opportunity to be a hero.</i>

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.250
Out!

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:05.140
Th-That was unlucky.

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:08.080
Aw, man, that was a great chance, too.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:10.880
All of a sudden, it's three outs.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:11.710
It's okay.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:12.850
Let's move on.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:15.970
This is our last turn to defend!

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:18.760
This is our chance to grab 
our first win of the tournament.

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:19.930
Let's lock this down!

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:20.960
Yes, sir!

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:24.060
Urabe, are you getting too tired to pitch?

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:27.360
We've got a lead, so we can 
swap in Matsubara if we need to.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.490
What?

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.690
What kind of ace doesn't go
for a complete game shutout?

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:38.120
Besides, if Matsubara was pitching, 
the anxiety would drain me even more.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:43.320
<i>Urabe </i>does <i>look a bit worn out, yeah.</i>

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:46.840
<i>But we've got a four-run lead, 
so I think we'll be okay.</i>

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:52.120
Ball!

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.390
Ball four!

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:05.310
Out!

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:07.290
<i>Ph-Phew.</i>

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:20.780
Ball!

00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:22.220
Ball four!

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:25.980
Crap, the bases are loaded.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:36.810
Ball.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.810
Ball four!

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.020
Sweet! He walked a runner home!

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:42.730
We clawed back a run!

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:45.160
This game isn't over yet!

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:48.880
Hey, Tashiro! Urabe's on the ropes here!

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:50.990
Can't you put in Matsubara?

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.730
Matsubara's pitching won't
 get us out of this situation.

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:56.680
And it'd be too much pressure 
for him if we threw him on now.

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:00.870
You're a mess.

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:06.250
Do you really think
you can beat Touto Boys like this?

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:07.960
Shut up!

00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:14.020
Oh well. Plenty of time to learn how 
to pace yourself after we've won.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:17.580
Bottom line, we had a four-run 
lead coming into the seventh.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:20.480
There's no way we can let this game slip.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:24.340
If you can't get the next batter out, 
we're playing our trump card.

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:26.040
Got it?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.110
Now's not the time for acting cool.

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.740
A-All right.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:32.860
Play!

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:34.880
<i>Our trump card, huh?</i>

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:37.010
<i>You've got to be kidding me.</i>

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:40.370
<i>Anything but that!</i>

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:42.580
Strike!

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:47.960
Strike two!

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:51.580
Wow. Looks like he's back in the game!

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:54.930
Yeah, he's suddenly pitching a lot better.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:59.180
<i>Urabe, do you really hate 
our trump card that much?</i>

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:04.770
Yes, two outs!

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.190
Just one more left!

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.600
What's going on?

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.870
Andy has a word with him,
and he's back to normal?

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:12.590
What in the world did Andy say to him?

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:16.180
<i>I shouldn't have hit that three-run homer.</i>

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:21.870
<i>Urabe lacks not only stamina, but also
focus when he's pitching with a big lead.</i>

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:25.790
<i>I just hope we can get through this 
without playing our trump card.</i>

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:28.330
Fukui, please get us a run!

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.520
<i>We just need one more out.</i>

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:40.560
Crap!

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:43.410
<i>It's not over yet.</i>

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.280
<i>If we stop him at first, the game's over.</i>

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:02.640
All right!

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:17.640
Safe!

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.260
We tied the game in the final inning!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.650
Tell me that didn't just happen, Daigo...

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:35.650
<i>What the...</i>

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:39.780
<i>What... did I just do?</i>

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:42.440
D-Daigo...

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:44.930
He was aiming for another out at first base.

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:49.420
But it looks like he took his eye 
off the ball at the last second.

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:52.660
It's good that he's being aggressive,

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:55.490
but when the bases are loaded 
and you have a three-run lead,

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.600
that's the kind of mistake 
you simply can't afford.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:02.160
After all, there's no cover for an outfielder.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:07.140
All right, let's get our runner on third 
home and wrap this game up!

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:08.600
Time out!

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:14.110
I didn't think this would happen, 
but it looks like we're tied.

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:16.350
Just shake it off and focus!

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:20.400
As long as we prevent a walk-off,
we'll still have plenty of chances to win!

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.620
U-Urabe?

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:27.140
Manager, I think it's time 
you switched out the pitcher.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.060
Urabe's head has gone.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.020
Switch in Matsubara, huh?

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:34.880
Matsubara can't handle
such a high-pressure situation.

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:38.280
I'm really sorry, Manager.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:41.830
I was going to let you in on it 
after we'd won our first game.

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:44.560
I'll pitch.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:45.810
Excuse me?

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:48.680
The two of us have been
 practicing in secret.

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:53.310
In junior baseball, a player is only allowed 
to pitch a total of seven innings per game.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.750
So with Urabe alone, we can't win 
our way through the tournament.

00:18:57.380 --> 00:19:02.570
Well, it's true that Urabe can't 
pitch anymore after this inning.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:05.830
I think we've got no choice 
but to let me pitch.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.100
Hey, Urabe.

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:11.490
You're no longer pitching, so put on the mask.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:14.520
I won't let them get a walk-off.

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:19.310
Why are you getting all serious, An-chan?

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:21.800
Who even cares about this game anymore?

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:27.100
Look at where our useless defense got us
after everything I did.

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:28.980
This whole thing is a joke.

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:31.940
Me and you defeating the Touto Boys 
all by ourselves is imposs—

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:34.230
Shut up and catch!

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:36.560
The game isn't over yet.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:57.460
Strike! Out!

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:59.690
Whoa, nice pitch!

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:02.410
We managed to prevent the walk-off.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:05.970
And Andy's actually not that bad.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:10.840
Yeah. He doesn't throw like a pitcher, 
but he has better control than Urabe.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:13.980
<i>Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:23.100
I-I'm really sorry, Manager.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:26.910
I made a mistake we can't recover from.

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:32.870
I'm supposed to bat first in the 10th, 
but please, send in a pinch hitter.

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:38.430
Sorry, I didn't catch that.

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:39.550
What did you say?

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.300
You heard him just fine. 
He asked you to send in a pinch—

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:44.260
I said, I didn't hear him!

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:45.790
Listen up, Daigo!

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:48.940
I told you I'd swap you out 
if I saw any halfhearted plays!

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.860
Your mistake just now wasn't even close, 
so there's no reason to swap you out!

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:54.890
B-But...

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:56.300
Just go!

00:20:56.300 --> 00:20:58.090
The game isn't over yet!

00:20:58.510 --> 00:21:01.060
Your mistake isn't one 
we can't recover from just yet!

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:02.950
So go out there and 
start the recovery process!

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:13.170
Tashiro...

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.280
I know.

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:19.600
I get that a kid can't get over 
a mistake like that so easily.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:24.030
But if I sub him out now
 and we end up losing,

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:28.050
that might be the last time 
we see Daigo in a baseball field.

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:30.970
Play!

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.010
<i>No.</i>

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:34.970
<i>I can't do this!</i>

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:37.980
<i>We just needed one more out.</i>

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:41.800
<i>But my error ruined everything.</i>

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:45.680
<i>How am I supposed to make up for that?</i>

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:49.240
<i>I'll never get over something like that!</i>

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:55.290
Strike!

00:21:58.490 --> 00:22:01.300
What are you swinging at, Daigo-kun?

00:22:03.980 --> 00:22:07.340
Don't fall apart just because your 
error allowed them to score.

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.670
We'll never be able to form a battery

00:22:09.670 --> 00:22:12.770
if you have the mental fortitude 
of a block of tofu, Daigo-kun.

00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:15.860
H-Hikaru?

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:01.790
I don't believe this.

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:03.490
What's Hikaru doing here?

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:06.090
Did he come all the way 
from Gunma for this game?

00:24:07.180 --> 00:24:08.240
Damn it.

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:10.010
This isn't the time
to feel sorry for myself!

00:24:10.660 --> 00:24:11.800
Listen, Hikaru.

00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:13.760
I know you didn't just come here to watch.

00:24:14.510 --> 00:24:18.060
If you do go up on that mound, I'll...

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
Battery Debut!

00:24:19.170 --> 00:24:21.600
Next time: "Battery Debut!"

00:24:22.050 --> 00:24:24.040
Run to the stage of your dreams!
